  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;MARI BIYA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mari Biya is the first Babur king to rule from Biu and defeated Fulani invaders from the Gombe Emirate."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAI BIU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mai Biu, also styled Kuthli, is a place ruled by the Babur/Bura people, with a history dating back to Abdullahi, known as Yamta-ra-Wala or Yamta the Great, who established his rule around 1535."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biu is a place ruled by the Babur/Bura people, with a history dating back to Abdullahi, known as Yamta-ra-Wala or Yamta the Great, who established his rule around 1535."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDULLAHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdullahi, later known as Yamta-ra-Wala or Yamta the Great, is the founder of the rulers of Biu, establishing his rule around 1535."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARI WATILA TAMPTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mari Watila Tampta is a ruler of Biu, reigning around 1670 when the region became known as a kingdom."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN MIZRAHI ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Mizrahi organization is a group founded in 1950 by Professor Pinkhos Churgin, an American rabbi and educator, and was described by The New York Times as a cultural link between Israel and America when it opened in 1955."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROFESSOR PINKHOS CHURGIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Professor Pinkhos Churgin is the founder of the American Mizrahi organization, an American rabbi and educator."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RABBI MEIR BAR-ILAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rabbi Meir Bar-Ilan, originally 'Meir Berlin', is a Religious Zionist leader who inspired the establishment of the American Mizrahi organization."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KUTHLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kuthli is another style or name for Mai Biu, a place ruled by the Babur/Bura people, with a history dating back to Abdullahi, known as Yamta-ra-Wala or Yamta the Great, who established his rule around 1535."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BABUR/BURA PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Babur/Bura people are the main ethnic group in Biu, related to the Kanuri people."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KANURI PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ETHNIC_GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Kanuri people are related to the Babur/Bura people, who are the main ethnic group in Biu."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YAMTA-RA-WALA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yamta-ra-Wala is another name for Abdullahi, who established his rule in Biu around 1535."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YAMTA THE GREAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yamta the Great is another name for Abdullahi, who established his rule in Biu around 1535."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE NEW YORK TIMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The New York Times is a newspaper that described the American Mizrahi organization as a cultural link between Israel and America when it opened in 1955."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISRAEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Israel is mentioned as the country linked to the American Mizrahi organization by The New York Times."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BERLIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Berlin is mentioned as the place where Rabbi Meir Bar-Ilan was trained in Orthodox seminaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELIGIOUS ZIONIST LEADER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Religious Zionist leader is the role held by Rabbi Meir Bar-Ilan, who inspired the establishment of the American Mizrahi organization."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECULAR ACADEMIC STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secular academic studies are part of the dual curriculum provided by the American Mizrahi organization, alongside religious Torah studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELIGIOUS TORAH STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Religious Torah studies are part of the dual curriculum provided by the American Mizrahi organization, alongside secular academic studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1-866-489-1188&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONTACT_NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1-866-489-1188 is a toll-free number for assistance with baby names."</data>
